            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "See https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/41074#issuecomment-5289910312.\r\n\r\nOne potential fix I considered is implementing a retry mechanism: if the buffer contains unresolved/malformed code lenses while the buffer remains unchanged, nvim could re-request them up to a maximum retry limit until the data becomes valid. \r\n\r\nThat said, it would be much cleaner to introduce this after we do a deeper refactor of `vim.lsp.Capability` (the layer managing automatic LSP data fetching for code lenses, inlay hints, etc.).",
